=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
After exhaustive live inspection of R6 and R7, no active fault was found in
either device. R6 and R7 both have all physical interfaces up with zero errors
and zero dropped packets. OSPF is fully converged: R6 holds three Full
adjacencies (to r4, r5, and r7) and R7 holds one Full adjacency (to r6). IP
forwarding is enabled, iptables has no FORWARD rules, rp_filter is disabled,
and no tc policing or shaping is configured. Both devices' routing tables are
complete — all expected intra-area, inter-area, and redistributed-external
prefixes are present with correct next-hops. Seven independent end-to-end
connectivity tests covering paths that transit R6 (pc0→r7, pc12→r7, r1→r7,
r4→r7, r5→r7, r7→r8, r7→r9) all returned 0% packet loss with TTL values
consistent with the correct number of forwarding hops. The FRR log on both
routers contains nothing but normal startup and OSPF DD negotiation messages.
The root cause of the night-shift alert was the normal OSPF reconvergence
period: FRR daemons on the lab started at 06:53:46 and OSPF adjacencies did
not reach Full state until 06:54:26–31 — a ~45-second window during which no
routes existed and all transit traffic through R6 would have failed. Once
convergence completed, full connectivity was automatically restored. No
corrective action is required; the network is healthy.
=== END ===
